scene W: There is a proper way in: a year of instruction, a promise made in front of everyone, a name written in the book.
scene U: {N} has read its arguments and its critics. The answers do not settle every question, but they hold up better than any others {N} has found.
scene B: Belonging to something this old would give {N} weight: a community, a say in its councils, people who keep their word.
scene R: Something happened in that hall last spring that {N} still cannot explain, and does not want to explain away.
scene G: Their seasons, their meals, their prayers for the dead: {N} has been living by half of them for a year already.
