scene: At a talk in a rented hall {N} meets a teacher with a quiet voice and a small, devoted circle. Afterwards {friend} says the teacher asked about {N} by name.
scene W: The circle has rules: early mornings, a set path of study, a promise of loyalty to the teacher. Order, after years of drifting.
scene U: {N} notices that the teacher answers every question with another question, and that the fees rise at each level of the path.
scene B: The inner circle are given rooms, titles and the teacher's ear. {N} can see exactly how one climbs.
scene R: The talk lit something in {N} that has been dark for years, and {N} wants more of it, now.
scene G: The circle lives together on an old farm and grows its own food. It looks like the life {N} has always pictured.
